{"componentChunkName":"component---src-templates-post-template-js","path":"/blog/2024-10-16-how-to-change-placeholder-color-in-react-js/","result":{"data":{"markdownRemark":{"excerpt":"Hi Friends 👋, Welcome To aHoisting! To change placeholder color in react js, you can set  in  . It will change placeholder color in react js. Today, I am going…","html":"<p>Hi Friends 👋,</p>\n<p>Welcome To aHoisting!</p>\n<p>To change placeholder color in react js, you can set <code class=\"language-text\">color: pink;</code> in  <code class=\"language-text\">.custom-input::placeholder</code>. It will change placeholder color in react js.</p>\n<p>Today, I am going to show you, how to change placeholder color in react js.</p>\n<p>Table of contents</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Install and create a new React app.</li>\n<li>Import react component.</li>\n<li>Create a Component.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Let’s start with the first step.</p>\n<h2>Step 1: Install and create a new React app.</h2>\n<p>First you have to install the React project. You should use <code class=\"language-text\">create-react-app</code> command to create a new React project.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\">npx create<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>react<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\ncd my<span class=\"token operator\">-</span>app\nnpm start</code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 2: Import react component.</h2>\n<p>After installing, you have to import your React component.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"react\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<h2>Step 3: Create a Component.</h2>\n<p>You can use <code class=\"language-text\">.custom-input::placeholder</code> to change placeholder color in react js.</p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>input\n      style<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>inputStyle<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n      placeholder<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Enter your text here...\"</span>\n        <span class=\"token comment\">// Add the placeholder style using inline CSS-in-JS</span>\n      className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"custom-input\"</span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">/</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>style<span class=\"token operator\">></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">\n        .custom-input::placeholder {\n          color: pink;\n        }\n      </span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>style<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n<span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span></code></pre></div>\n<h2>Change placeholder color example.</h2>\n<p>The below code is an example of a React. You have to import <code class=\"language-text\">react</code> and set <code class=\"language-text\">color: pink;</code> in  <code class=\"language-text\">.custom-input::placeholder</code> to change placeholder color in react js.</p>\n<p><code class=\"language-text\">App.js</code></p>\n<div class=\"gatsby-highlight\" data-language=\"js\"><pre class=\"language-js\"><code class=\"language-js\"><span class=\"token keyword\">import</span> React <span class=\"token keyword\">from</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"react\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">function</span> <span class=\"token function\">App</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">const</span> inputStyle <span class=\"token operator\">=</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">color</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"black\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span> <span class=\"token comment\">// Text color</span>\n    <span class=\"token literal-property property\">fontSize</span><span class=\"token operator\">:</span> <span class=\"token string\">\"16px\"</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">,</span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n\n  <span class=\"token keyword\">return</span> <span class=\"token punctuation\">(</span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>input\n        style<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span>inputStyle<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n        placeholder<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"Enter your text here...\"</span>\n        <span class=\"token comment\">// Add the placeholder style using inline CSS-in-JS</span>\n        className<span class=\"token operator\">=</span><span class=\"token string\">\"custom-input\"</span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">/</span><span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n      <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span>style<span class=\"token operator\">></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">{</span><span class=\"token template-string\"><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span><span class=\"token string\">\n        .custom-input::placeholder {\n          color: pink;\n        }\n      </span><span class=\"token template-punctuation string\">`</span></span><span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span><span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>style<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n    <span class=\"token operator\">&lt;</span><span class=\"token operator\">/</span>div<span class=\"token operator\">></span>\n  <span class=\"token punctuation\">)</span><span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span>\n<span class=\"token punctuation\">}</span>\n\n<span class=\"token keyword\">export</span> <span class=\"token keyword\">default</span> App<span class=\"token punctuation\">;</span></code></pre></div>\n<p>In the above code example, I have used the <code class=\"language-text\">color: pink;</code> to change placeholder color in react js.</p>\n<p>Check the output of the above code.</p>\n<p><span\n      class=\"gatsby-resp-image-wrapper\"\n      style=\"position: relative; display: block; margin-left: auto; margin-right: auto; max-width: 406px; \"\n    >\n      <a\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-link\"\n    href=\"/static/d8d2e0727fad131bc925b4131ac001df/09a6f/placeholder-color.webp\"\n    style=\"display: block\"\n    target=\"_blank\"\n    rel=\"noopener\"\n  >\n    <span\n    class=\"gatsby-resp-image-background-image\"\n    style=\"padding-bottom: 62.0253164556962%; position: relative; bottom: 0; left: 0; background-image: url('data:image/webp;base64,UklGRkgAAABXRUJQVlA4IDwAAABQAwCdASoUAAwAPtFipk0oJiOiMAgBABoJQBOj+ABgaLbIiADeZ874np7i83/cQQpGBct45BGn1ioTAAA='); background-size: cover; display: block;\"\n  ></span>\n  <img\n        class=\"gatsby-resp-image-image\"\n        alt=\"React, placeholder, color\"\n        title=\"React, placeholder, color\"\n        src=\"/static/d8d2e0727fad131bc925b4131ac001df/09a6f/placeholder-color.webp\"\n        srcset=\"/static/d8d2e0727fad131bc925b4131ac001df/81b7c/placeholder-color.webp 158w,\n/static/d8d2e0727fad131bc925b4131ac001df/6ea66/placeholder-color.webp 315w,\n/static/d8d2e0727fad131bc925b4131ac001df/09a6f/placeholder-color.webp 406w\"\n        sizes=\"(max-width: 406px) 100vw, 406px\"\n        style=\"width:100%;height:100%;margin:0;vertical-align:middle;position:absolute;top:0;left:0;\"\n        loading=\"lazy\"\n        decoding=\"async\"\n      />\n  </a>\n    </span></p>\n<p>All the best 👍</p>","frontmatter":{"title":"How to change placeholder color in React js?","tags":["React"],"date":"October 16, 2024","description":"Example of change placeholder color in react js with step by step tutorial - aHoisting","social_image":{"absolutePath":"/Users/mac/Documents/hoisting/ahoisting/static/media/template/reactjs.jpg"}}},"prev":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to change radio button color in react js?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-10-20-how-to-change-radio-button-color-in-react-js/"}},"next":{"frontmatter":{"title":"How to change paragraph alignment in react js?"},"fields":{"slug":"/blog/2024-10-15-how-to-change-paragraph-alignment-in-react-js/"}}},"pageContext":{"slug":"/blog/2024-10-16-how-to-change-placeholder-color-in-react-js/","prevSlug":"/blog/2024-10-20-how-to-change-radio-button-color-in-react-js/","nextSlug":"/blog/2024-10-15-how-to-change-paragraph-alignment-in-react-js/"}},"staticQueryHashes":["2555585279","2714594843","3159585216"]}